$abs(x_2 - a) < epsilon_1 = abs(x_1 - a)/2$ \
$abs(x_3 - a) < epsilon_3 = abs(x_3 - a)/2$
$=> abs(x_n - a) < epsilon_n = abs(x_(n+1) + a)/2 => abs(x_n - a) < abs(x_1 - a)/2^(n-1)$ \
